examples.question_text:
Classify each marked angle.

(a)
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (2.2,0)--(0,0)--(65:2.2);
\draw (0.55,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=65,radius=0.55];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(b)
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2.2,0)--(0,0)--(50:2.2);
\draw (50:0.55) arc[start angle=50,end angle=180,radius=0.55];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(c)
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2.2,0)--(0,0)--(0,2.2);
\draw (-0.35,0)--(-0.35,0.35)--(0,0.35);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Classify the marked angle. Use the arc to identify the turn being shown.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (2.2,0)--(0,0)--(120:2.2);
\draw (120:0.65) arc[start angle=120,end angle=360,radius=0.65];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
